<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for LOCAL macOS builds only (see the `build:local` script).

  Entitlements.mac.plist — the file CI uses — declares restricted capabilities:
  a team identifier, iCloud/CloudKit containers, aps-environment, and an
  application group. Those are only valid when the app is signed with a real
  Developer ID and a matching provisioning profile. Signed ad-hoc instead, the
  kernel refuses to authorize them and kills the process at launch
  (SIGKILL, exit 137, no crash report — `spctl -a -t exec` reports "rejected").

  An empty entitlement set is correct here: this build is not sandboxed, so the
  App Sandbox entitlements in the CI file are inert anyway, and the features
  they gate (microphone, calendars) are governed at runtime by TCC plus the
  usage-description strings in Info.plist.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
